{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02700",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 3.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Lovely to meet you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.86,
      "end_seconds": 9.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Alright, no problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.5,
      "end_seconds": 26.91,
      "duration_seconds": 12.41,
      "text": "I've been dealing with my heart suddenly racing. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.7,
      "end_seconds": 29.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.16,
      "end_seconds": 41.4,
      "duration_seconds": 11.24,
      "text": "It's been like this since Friday. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.94,
      "end_seconds": 47.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.77,
      "end_seconds": 51.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "I'd say every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.46,
      "end_seconds": 56.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.41,
      "end_seconds": 69.45,
      "duration_seconds": 12.04,
      "text": "A pounding in my neck goes along with it, most of the time. The pounding in my neck? That's been since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.17,
      "end_seconds": 73.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.37,
      "end_seconds": 80.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Just a mole taken off my arm, a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.45,
      "end_seconds": 99.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.37,
      "end_seconds": 109.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "Sorry, you know, what was I saying, I've had heart disease for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.58,
      "end_seconds": 122.53,
      "duration_seconds": 11.95,
      "text": "Right, so heart disease is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.67,
      "end_seconds": 128.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.17,
      "end_seconds": 133.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.81,
      "end_seconds": 152.26,
      "duration_seconds": 17.45,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I've never touched a cigarette. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.91,
      "end_seconds": 156.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Is there any regular medication you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.58,
      "end_seconds": 161.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "So, no, I'm not on anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.97,
      "end_seconds": 173.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Has there been any fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.1,
      "end_seconds": 177.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "No, none, no fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.68,
      "end_seconds": 185.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any breathlessness, family history of sudden death or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.96,
      "end_seconds": 189.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.66,
      "end_seconds": 193.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.64,
      "end_seconds": 197.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.44,
      "end_seconds": 203.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.83,
      "end_seconds": 215.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.93,
      "end_seconds": 242.93,
      "duration_seconds": 10.0,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 108 over 73, temp 36.4 degrees, pulse is 76 beats a minute, saturation 97 percent, respiratory rate 16."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.31,
      "end_seconds": 245.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.47,
      "end_seconds": 250.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.39,
      "end_seconds": 255.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.41,
      "end_seconds": 259.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.29,
      "end_seconds": 274.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.22,
      "end_seconds": 291.15,
      "duration_seconds": 10.93,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Right, here's what I'm thinking. This is probably episodes of supraventricular tachycardia. Atrial fibrillation is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.94,
      "end_seconds": 306.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Let's book an ECG to look into palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 307.16,
      "end_seconds": 312.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "We have a slot Monday at 3:30 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.81,
      "end_seconds": 322.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.74,
      "text": "Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. I'm going to send a referral to the cardiology clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.16,
      "end_seconds": 323.86,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.5,
      "end_seconds": 345.62,
      "duration_seconds": 21.12,
      "text": "A 7-day heart monitor is something we might do if this doesn't improve next month. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait. We'll catch up after the monitor. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.32,
      "end_seconds": 350.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Actually, um, great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}